From 3d264b2019f10323b4561a6af22348312ec897fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John O'Dell <johncodell14@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 22:55:08 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Freeciv45 right edge: notification badges that go to the city
 or tile and clear on click

Under the right-edge column's buttons, each unvisited message that has a
place to go gets a round 36 px badge, newest at the top: as many as fit
below the buttons, at most eight, then a "+N" badge for the rest. The
badge's icon and border colour say the message's kind (city, diplomacy,
military, research or other, from the event's section of the message
options), its tooltip is the message text.

A click goes there and marks the message visited, which removes the badge
and puts the message in italics in the messages log: an own city's event
opens the city overlay (meswin_popup_city), any other centres the map on
the tile (meswin_goto) and closes an open overlay first. "+N" closes the
overlay, returns to the map and scrolls the messages log to the oldest
message that has no badge.

The badges follow the message list: real_meswin_dialog_update refreshes
them, and so does a click on a message in the log. The column refills them
when its height changes. common/events.h now exports the event sections
(enum event_section_n) and get_event_section(), which were private to
events.c. Themed in the NightStalker and System resource.qss.

panels.md section 8.2, issue 143.
